e0ce25-445d-58ee-9787-78746dffa9e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-87153" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The amount of water per month consumed by a randomly selected person\n- The number of pages in a particular book\n- The amount of time that a randomly selected person spends waiting for a particular bus" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040017/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. The number of pages in a particular book is not the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\n- Statement III describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ed578d21-e7bc-53f7-9966-bc58c20b1c26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "eb4ed27d-8f1e-5a94-ae15-0d8ad8cc6f0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "464fb7ed-f856-5245-9633-4bbf6e183eb3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9a7bc289-8212-5870-a4bb-d6e4f1287766" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e3f8be16-82d0-514f-bbd6-ff667c3c5eeb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb53937-43f9-50c6-bc3e-cf9dcd50432a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87155/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-87155/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-87155/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-87155/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-87155/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-87155/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87155" :question/id #uuid "206f3fcf-ad34-5fea-b36b-6dd22be1a9ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-87155" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The score when a roulette wheel is spun at random\n- The amount of water consumed by a randomly selected person on a particular day, measured in liters\n- The number of students in a particular class on a randomly selected day" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040017/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible outcomes do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,…,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87155/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87155"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-86911"] :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The percent concentration of fruit concentrate in a randomly selected fruit drink\n- The number of times a coin is flipped until it lands on tails\n- The number of days in a particular week" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040017/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,100]$ (since the concentration can be anywhere between $0%$ and $100%$).\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $1,2,3,…,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a continuous random variable. The number of days in a particular week is not the outcome of a trial or experiment. (By definition, there are $7$ days in a week.)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-87160/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "6d2377dc-878d-5277-996f-e7edfffaf2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87160/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1cf9c9af-a111-59cb-83ca-9fffd32ae6a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87160/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #